+/*
+ * mscoree as the shim of the .NET Framework
+ *
+ * Since Windows 8 mscoree.dll is a file of the system, not of the .NET
+ * Framework: a shim whose every export goes on to mscoreei.dll of the
+ * installed Framework (InstallRoot\v4.0.30319), which picks and starts the
+ * runtime. The Framework's installer, made for Windows 8 and later, brings
+ * mscoreei.dll and the runtime but no mscoree.dll, so this is the one a
+ * .NET program finds. With the Framework installed, each export below jumps
+ * to mscoreei's; without it, to Wine's own (Mono), as before. Exports
+ * mscoreei has not got (_CorValidateImage, _CorImageUnloading, and Wine's
+ * registration) are always Wine's.
